  "question": {
    "text": "The shortest wavelength of the spectral lines in the Lyman series of hydrogen spectrum is $915 Ã…$. The longest wavelength of spectral lines in the Balmer series will be _____ $Ã…$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6588",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0018_99af96f2a954.png\"><br />Shortest, $\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda}=-13.6\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_1^2}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_2^2}\\right)$\n$\\lambda \\downarrow \\mathrm{E} \\uparrow ; \\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda_0}=-13.6(1)$\nBalmer Series :<img src=\"assets\\st0018_4101d4fc36fd.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda_1}=-13.6\\left(\\frac{1}{2^2}-\\frac{1}{3^2}\\right) \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda_1}=-13.6\\left(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{9}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda_1}=-13.6 \\times\\left(\\frac{5}{36}\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\frac{-13.6 \\lambda_0}{\\lambda_1}=-13.6 \\times \\frac{5}{36} \\\\ & \\lambda_1=\\frac{\\lambda_0 \\times 36}{5}=\\frac{915 \\times 36}{5}=6588\\end{aligned}$"
